    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Sorensen&#x27;s 1909 definition \mathrm{pH} = -\log_{10}[H^+] (~chemistrykit.solutions.systems.acid_base.ph_from_h) turns hydrogen-ion concentrations spanning fourteen orders of magnitude into numbers between 0 and 14. Below, the pH of several everyday solutions is computed from their equilibrium [H^+] and placed on the scale, and the companion relation \mathrm{pH} + \mathrm{pOH} = pK_w = 14 is checked with poh_from_oh.">

